# Window: a persistent snapshot writing table data to its .vpt file.
#   DefaultSnapshotDataTarget queues each compressed block on its write
#   service; the anonymous Callable ($3, the third anonymous class in the
#   source) rate-limits, then writes the block with FileChannel.write inside
#   a try whose IOException handler marks the target failed.
#
# Fault: the next FileChannel.write of that block throws IOException, as a
#   real disk error (EIO, ENOSPC) would, for snapshots whose nonce starts
#   with BYTEMAN_. Only the snapshot-io-error nemesis uses that prefix, so
#   command log truncation snapshots (where VoltDB deliberately crashes the
#   node on an IOException) and other snapshots are not touched.
#
# Correct behaviour: the snapshot is reported failed (@Statistics
#   SNAPSHOTSTATUS RESULT=FAILURE, "Failed to take snapshot <nonce>" in
#   volt.log), no node crashes, and the cluster keeps serving.
#
# Why two rules: Byteman raises a rule's exception from handler code it
# appends to the trigger method, outside that method's own try blocks, so a
# throw placed in the Callable itself skips its catch and finally (the target
# is never marked failed, its buffers leak and close() waits forever). The
# throw therefore happens in the callee, FileChannelImpl.write, and reaches
# the Callable at its call site like a real IOException. The first rule tags
# the snapshot write thread just before that call; the second fires only on
# a tagged thread and clears the tag.
#
# The $3 class name follows the source order of anonymous classes in
# DefaultSnapshotDataTarget. If it changes, the rules stop matching and never
# fire, which the nemesis reports as a failure.

RULE snapshot-write-ioexception tag
CLASS org.voltdb.DefaultSnapshotDataTarget$3
METHOD call
AT INVOKE org.voltdb.NativeSnapshotDataTarget.enforceSnapshotRateLimit
IF $0.this$0.m_nonce.startsWith("BYTEMAN_")
DO link("snapshot-write-ioexception", Thread.currentThread(),
        $0.this$0.m_nonce + " file=" + $0.this$0)
ENDRULE

RULE snapshot-write-ioexception throw
CLASS sun.nio.ch.FileChannelImpl
METHOD write(java.nio.ByteBuffer)
AT ENTRY
IF linked("snapshot-write-ioexception", Thread.currentThread()) != null
DO traceln("BYTEMAN snapshot-write-ioexception fired nonce="
           + unlink("snapshot-write-ioexception", Thread.currentThread()));
   throw new java.io.IOException("Byteman snapshot-write-ioexception (injected)")
ENDRULE
